  "body": "What happens: the release gate tier for the 0.19.0 cut is red in the app heavy lane (release, `--ignored`). In `camcraft-app` `--test operations`:\n\n- `swarf_generates_blade_lying_axes_and_verifies_clean_full_band`\n- `advanced_swarf_adds_the_coarse_rungs_full_band`\n\nboth fail in `verifies_clean` (`crates/app/tests/operations.rs:4896`): \"SWA must verify with zero blocking warnings\" (and \"SW1 ...\"), with the same 18 hits in both:\n`SweepHit { at: 2108, part: false }`, 2159, 2215, 2277, 2344, 2405, 2474, 2535, 2605, 2662, 2714, 2762, 2827, 2887, 2949, 3008, 3070, 3129 (all `part: false`, about every 50-70 moves).\n\nExpected: the swarf path verifies with no blocking warning, as it did at the v0.18.0 cut.\n\nNot known yet, and the first thing to find out: whether the swarf path changed (a real sweep contact that must stay refused, then the generator is wrong) or the sweep check changed (a false refusal of a legal path). Either way the post is blocked for these ops, so nothing unsafe is posted; a legal program refused is the lesser reading, a generator regression the worse one.\n\nEvidence: `gate-logs/release-20261113-113616/12-app_heavy_lane_release_--ignored_.log` line 1129, tree `9047b5f6f` (main `38699549e` plus release docs). The tests are `#[ignore]`d release-lane, so the quick and batch tiers never ran them.\n\nRerun: `cargo test --release -p camcraft-app --test operations -- --ignored swarf`\n\nDone means: the commit that turned these red is named (bisect between `v0.18.0` and main); the cause is fixed in the generator or in the check, with the reason written here; both tests pass in release without loosening `verifies_clean` or allowing a blocking warning through; if the hits are real contacts, the path is fixed, not the verdict.\n\nBlocks the 0.19.0 cut.\n",
